<title>UK: ISO cuts estimate for 1996/97 world sugar output.</title>
<headline>ISO cuts estimate for 1996/97 world sugar output.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Sugar Organization (ISO) on Monday estimated world sugar production at 123.6 million tonnes raw value for 1996/97, down from its previous forecast of 123.79 million. The revised figure would exceeed consumption by nearly three million tonnes, the ISO said.  </p>
<p>In its earlier estimate of the world 1996/97 balance issued in October, the ISO pegged consumption at 121.29 million tonnes, leaving a statistical surplus of 2.50 million. Full details of the ISO's second and revised estimate for the 1996/97 global sugar balance would be released on December 13, it said.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
